1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,275
This is OkurmenKIDS: a production education
technology platform for a children's

2
00:00:06,315 --> 00:00:09,376
programming academy in Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan.

3
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:14,851
It is not a tutorial project. It is a live
system used by trainers, assistants,

4
00:00:14,891 --> 00:00:17,088
managers, students and parents.

5
00:00:17,388 --> 00:00:21,934
In this video, I'll walk through every
production service, the backend behind them,

6
00:00:21,974 --> 00:00:23,616
and how it all is deployed.

7
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:30,461
OkurmenKIDS is one repository with four
applications that share a single backend.

8
00:00:30,761 --> 00:00:33,953
The public website lives at okurmenkids.com.

9
00:00:34,253 --> 00:00:39,123
The learning management system is at
lms.okurmenkids.com.

10
00:00:39,423 --> 00:00:45,305
The Django administration panel is at
api.okurmenkids.com, slash admin.

11
00:00:45,605 --> 00:00:51,059
The Django REST API itself answers at
api.okurmenkids.com.

12
00:00:51,359 --> 00:00:55,697
And the exam training portal is at
training.okurmenkids.com.

13
00:00:55,997 --> 00:01:01,585
The three React frontends are deployed
independently on Vercel, and all of them
talk

14
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:05,460
to one Django backend on Railway, backed by
PostgreSQL.

15
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:11,833
The public website is the academy's front
door: a React 19 and TypeScript single

16
00:01:11,873 --> 00:01:14,157
page application built with Vite.

17
00:01:14,457 --> 00:01:17,389
It is available in Russian, Kyrgyz and
English.

18
00:01:17,689 --> 00:01:22,850
Courses, student projects, achievements,
news, events and the team are not

19
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:30,069
hard-coded. They come from the public site
API and are managed by the marketing team
inside the LMS.

20
00:01:30,369 --> 00:01:35,365
When a parent books a trial lesson, the
request is posted to the API as a lead.

21
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:43,256
The LMS is the operational core of the
academy. Staff sign in, and access is role-
based.

22
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:48,398
The backend defines roles such as trainer,
team lead, assistant, accountant,

23
00:01:48,438 --> 00:01:54,111
director, operations, HR and marketing, plus
one role for students and their parents.

24
00:01:54,411 --> 00:01:59,648
Each role has its own cabinet: lessons,
attendance, homework, exams, scholarships,

25
00:01:59,688 --> 00:02:02,155
salaries, recruitment and marketing.

26
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:07,215
Those cabinets hold private student data, so
I'm only showing the public pages of

27
00:02:07,255 --> 00:02:08,650
the same application.

28
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:14,095
This is the public schedule: a read-only
timetable by day, week, room and trainer,

29
00:02:14,135 --> 00:02:18,371
served from a cached public endpoint with a
whitelist of fields.

30
00:02:21,633 --> 00:02:26,776
Here is the gallery of student projects
published by trainers, and the academy news
feed.

31
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:35,886
The LMS is also an installable progressive
web app with web push notifications.

32
00:02:37,133 --> 00:02:43,749
Next to the API runs the Django
administration panel, themed with Jazzmin
and a custom dashboard.

33
00:02:44,049 --> 00:02:48,093
In production it sits behind a login, and I
won't sign in on camera.

34
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:52,861
To show what it manages, this is the same
admin running locally on an empty

35
00:02:52,901 --> 00:02:54,329
development database.

36
00:02:54,629 --> 00:03:00,076
Accounting and payroll, the student and
parent portal, marketing, news, operations,

37
00:03:00,116 --> 00:03:05,100
recruitment, testing, the website CMS and
more. Every section comes from the

38
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:09,520
backend's own Django apps, and access
follows staff permissions.

39
00:03:10,767 --> 00:03:17,936
The API host is api.okurmenkids.com. Its
root path returns 404 by design: every

40
00:03:17,976 --> 00:03:24,605
route lives under api slash v1, and the
health check returns status ok.

41
00:03:24,867 --> 00:03:31,373
It is built with Django REST Framework and
JWT authentication, and documented with

42
00:03:31,413 --> 00:03:35,315
an OpenAPI schema generated by drf-
spectacular.

43
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:44,981
The production schema currently describes
724 paths and 966 operations, across 28
Django apps.

44
00:03:45,281 --> 00:03:49,776
Academy, billing, accounting, testing,
training, attendance, scholarships,

45
00:03:49,816 --> 00:03:53,521
recruitment, operations, marketing and the
public website.

46
00:03:53,767 --> 00:04:00,429
Public endpoints need no login, are
throttled per IP address, and return only
whitelisted fields.

47
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:06,625
The training portal helps students prepare
for exams. There is no registration: a

48
00:04:06,665 --> 00:04:08,420
student types only a name.

49
00:04:09,733 --> 00:04:14,778
Tests come from the backend's testing
module, with single choice, multiple choice,

50
00:04:14,818 --> 00:04:18,688
text and code questions, and an explanation
for each answer.

51
00:04:18,988 --> 00:04:23,310
The time limit and the grading are enforced
on the server, not in the browser.

52
00:04:23,567 --> 00:04:28,925
There are also curated videos, study
materials and a leaderboard. The interface
is

53
00:04:28,965 --> 00:04:32,867
in Kyrgyz, and every piece of content comes
from the API.

54
00:04:34,133 --> 00:04:36,331
Here is the high-level architecture.

55
00:04:36,631 --> 00:04:41,967
Three React and TypeScript frontends, the
public website, the LMS and the training

56
00:04:42,007 --> 00:04:46,746
portal, are separate Vercel projects, so
each one ships independently.

57
00:04:47,046 --> 00:04:53,703
They all call one Django REST API on
Railway, and the Django admin is served by
the same backend.

58
00:04:54,004 --> 00:05:00,410
The backend ships as a Docker image on
Python 3.12 with Gunicorn and WhiteNoise. On

59
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:06,779
start, it collects static files and applies
migrations under a PostgreSQL advisory

60
00:05:06,819 --> 00:05:09,687
lock, so only one replica migrates.

61
00:05:09,987 --> 00:05:15,442
Data lives in PostgreSQL, and uploaded media
is stored on a Railway volume.

62
00:05:15,742 --> 00:05:21,138
Background work is written as Celery tasks.
Celery can use a Redis broker; without

63
00:05:21,178 --> 00:05:27,890
one, tasks run synchronously, and a Railway
cron job runs the scheduled tasks every
thirty minutes.

64
00:05:28,190 --> 00:05:34,045
The backend also drives headless Chromium
through Playwright to render report images
for parents.

65
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:41,095
The stack: Python, Django and Django REST
Framework. PostgreSQL. Celery, with Redis

66
00:05:41,135 --> 00:05:42,832
as an optional broker.

67
00:05:43,132 --> 00:05:48,103
React, TypeScript and Vite on the frontend.
Docker for the backend image, Railway

68
00:05:48,143 --> 00:05:51,510
for the backend, and Vercel for the three
frontends.

69
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:58,447
I work on OkurmenKIDS as a full stack
developer and Python backend developer, from

70
00:05:58,487 --> 00:06:04,357
Django models and REST APIs to React
interfaces, Docker and production
deployment.

71
00:06:04,657 --> 00:06:08,949
The source code is on GitHub, and more of my
work is on my GitHub profile.

72
00:06:09,249 --> 00:06:13,950
Building real-world software products, from
backend architecture to production

73
00:06:13,990 --> 00:06:16,086
deployment. Thanks for watching.
